codex
The source evidence now pins the critical mechanics: OpenSSH turns each SOCKS `CONNECT` into a `direct-tcpip` request; the authenticated server-side `sshd` worker checks forwarding policy, resolves any supplied hostname with remote `getaddrinfo`, and opens the destination TCP socket as the SSH login user. I’m setting up a loopback-only synthetic SSH/HTTP fixture to reproduce that path without touching either production configuration or an external destination.
