Key finding: `ssh -D` is an application-level TCP SOCKS proxy. The remote `sshd` worker resolves/connects, so remote VPN routing works only when its route and process/user policy admit that worker. It does not provide source-Mac system routing or UDP. [OpenSSH documentation](https://man.openbsd.org/ssh#-D), [Apple VPN routing](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/networkextension/routing-your-vpn-network-traffic).

